  "difficulty_reason": "Beyond the ordinary Sobolev and Birkhoff normal-form prerequisites, the authored proof establishes cluster-sensitive weighted Poisson-bracket estimates for an infinite family of super-actions. The separation lemma forces a lower bound on the third largest frequency and converts this into the high-frequency decay factor. It then couples the weighted estimates to a symplectic change of variables and high-order Hamiltonian remainder under a long-time bootstrap; this residual argument exceeds ordinary doctoral PDE qualifying exercises.",
